I hate tiles too.  I run the Qt version w/o tiles.  There are two ways
to set it to ASCII.  The easier and more temporary is to type
<shift-o> <a> <enter>.  More complicated, and more permanent, is to
set up a preferences file at "~/Library/Preferences/NetHack
Defaults.txt".  If you want, you can just put in a single line that
reads "OPTIONS=ascii_map".  Mine looks like this:

# Move this file to your 'Library/Preferences' folder
OPTIONS=number_pad,menustyle:partial,showexp,ascii_map
OPTIONS=hilite_pet,toptenwin,msghistory:1000,windowtype:Qt
OPTIONS=autodig,!mail,rest_on_space,standout,time
OPTIONS=!tombstone,color,fruit:mango,pickup_burden:B
OPTIONS=catname:Mac,dogname:Akai,horsename:Trigger
OPTIONS=gender:female,name:Thane,
OPTIONS=!splash_screen
#OPTIONS=race:Gnome,role:Wizard,align:neutral
#OPTIONS=race:Human,role:Valk,align:neutral
OPTIONS=race:Human,role:Monk,align:neutral
OPTIONS=!cmdassist,pickup_types:/=?!$+"
qt_tilewidth=13
qt_tileheight=22
qt_fontsize=l

-- thane

